    "knowledge_point_id": "f3bd5e5c-b8d1-53e5-9968-8bef8faceb4b",
    "knowledge_point": "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing the Tangent Function Transformed by Multiple Operations",
    "problem": "Consider the equation $\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘})-\\sqrt{3}=0$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ If the exact solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are written in ascending order, what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$",
    "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘})-\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘}) & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘}) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘}) & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-{45}^{∘} & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={45}^{∘}+{45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 2x & ={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {90}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={45}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={135}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x={225}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x={315}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx={45}^{∘},{135}^{∘},{225}^{∘},{315}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is $45\\cdot 135=6\\,075.$",
